<chapter xml:id="ch-primes" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Factors, Primes and Proofs</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      This chapter delves deeper into whole numbers and their properties.
      We will see that we can write whole numbers as products of other numbers.
      Recall that if a number can be written as the product between 1 and itself then it is prime.
      Understanding how to break down any whole number into its prime factors is a key mathematical concept and in a practical sense will help when we tackle adding fractions in Chapter \ref{ch:fractions}.
    </p>

    <p>
      As we build up the concepts of prime numbers and their properties, we also will spend some time on formal and informal mathematical \textbf{proofs}.
    </p>
  </introduction>

